E AX3049 374-restrict-no-foreign.ax:23:6-13 restriction-violated "`bridges` claims `restrict(no-foreign)` and the body reaches the `extern` item `add`: bridges -> add" ?"a restriction is a CLAIM the author wrote, and this is the compiler answering it. `no-io`, `no-alloc`, `no-foreign` and `no-cast:deep` are transitive - the effect row and the call graph are fixpoints over every callee - and the path in the message is the chain of resolved calls (`symbols --calls` spells each hop the same way) from this declaration to where the effect enters, so the fix is at a named place rather than somewhere below. Make the body keep the claim, or delete the tag, which WITHDRAWS the claim rather than answering it; an unrestricted function is never asked"
E AX3049 374-restrict-no-foreign.ax:34:6-15 restriction-violated "`viaHelper` claims `restrict(no-foreign)` and the body reaches the `extern` item `add`: viaHelper -> wrap -> add" ?"a restriction is a CLAIM the author wrote, and this is the compiler answering it. `no-io`, `no-alloc`, `no-foreign` and `no-cast:deep` are transitive - the effect row and the call graph are fixpoints over every callee - and the path in the message is the chain of resolved calls (`symbols --calls` spells each hop the same way) from this declaration to where the effect enters, so the fix is at a named place rather than somewhere below. Make the body keep the claim, or delete the tag, which WITHDRAWS the claim rather than answering it; an unrestricted function is never asked"
